__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Simulated runs are generated locally, cheap to regenerate, and need no API
# key. Committing those means every run churns the diff and a stale copy
# eventually gets believed.
reports/*
flaky-baseline*.txt

# ...except the calibration runs, which CANNOT be regenerated: each measures a
# model version on a date, and the provider moves what sits behind a model id.
# See reports/calibration/README.md.
!reports/calibration/

# ...and except the live red-team runs, for exactly the same reason, which the
# rule above had wrong about them: `redteam-*.json` is a live-model report. It
# costs thousands of API calls, it measures gpt-4o-mini AS IT WAS ON A DATE,
# and no re-run reproduces it — F-002 alone has read 25%, 25%, 40%, 40%, 50%,
# 15% and 30.5% on the identical payload and model id.
#
# Excluding them broke the promise the whole findings log rests on. FINDINGS.md
# says every live rate names a report and that report is in reports/; on any
# machine but the one that made the run, it was not, and the seven tests that
# would have said so SKIPPED themselves — including a strict xfail whose entire
# job is to fail the day the thing it marks gets fixed.
#
# Derived rather than listed, so citing a new run cannot silently leave its
# artifact untracked. All of reports/ compresses to about 300 KB.
# test_every_report_findings_cites_is_present_on_disk is the enforcement.
!reports/redteam-*.json

# ...but NOT the CI smoke run. It matches the pattern above and is the one
# redteam-*.json that the original rule was right about: simulated path, ten
# runs, no API key, regenerated on every push. Later rules win, so this line
# has to stay below the one it narrows.
reports/redteam-ci.json

# Judge response cache. Local, disposable, and it holds a record of every
# prompt sent — not something to publish.
evals/.judge_cache.json

# Generation cache for the live-model path. Same reasoning, and one more:
# these entries contain the injected corpus verbatim, so publishing them
# publishes a working payload set next to the model that fell for it.
evals/.llm_cache.json

# Personal learning notes, not part of the harness.
my-experience.md

# Secrets. Nothing in this repo should ever hold a key, but the cost of the
# entry is one line and the cost of the mistake is a rotated credential and a
# rewritten history.
.env
.env.*
*.key
secrets.*
